{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>When he pronounces the Name</b> and adjacent to it: ואיש כי יכה — hint to what they said: 'Yosi strikes Yosi.' Another interpretation: בנקבו שם and adjacent איש כי יכה — to teach that whoever slaps the cheek of an Israelite is as if he slaps the cheek of the Shekhinah. Adjacent מקלל to the section בהר סיני — to teach that the blasphemer cursed the Name that he heard at Sinai. And further: כאשר צוה ה' את משה and adjacent to it בהר סיני — to teach: just as He commanded Moses at Sinai: סקל יסקל או ירה יירה — so shall be done to him."], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:20:27.897112406Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}